<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">26 Baku Commissars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The 26 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baku">Baku</a> Commissars were Bolshevik and Left Socialist Revolutionary leaders of the Baku Commune, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stepan-shaumian">Stepan Shaumian</a>, who governed Baku in 1918. After the commune fell in July 1918 they tried to escape by sea but were taken to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmenbasy">Krasnovodsk</a>, held by the anti-Bolshevik Transcaspian government, and shot in the desert on 20 September 1918. Soviet propaganda made them revolutionary martyrs and blamed their deaths on British officers.</p></div>
